  data: {
    LLM: "Don't put all your best cards in one hand. Winning one comparison and losing two will lose you the round. Aim for three balanced 'Pairs' rather than one 'Prial' and two junk hands.\n\nThe 'Middle' Trap: Many players put their second-best cards in the middle hand. If you put your best cards in the middle, you can often steal a point from someone who played traditionally.\n\nRange Splitting: Evaluate the deck's remaining strength. If you hold many Spades, expect opponents to be weak in sequences and strong in pairs. Adjust your partition to beat pairs with low sequences (Runs).",
